{"name":"Bovine","hex":"#52585c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bovine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or characteristic of cattle, buffaloes, or bison.","Belonging to the subfamily Bovinae."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal of a family, subfamily, tribe, or genera including cattle, buffaloes and bison.","An animal of the subfamily Bovinae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bovine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bovinae","blocks":[{"text":"Bovines comprise a diverse group of 10 genera of medium to large-sized ungulates, including cattle, bison, African buffalo, water buffalos, and the four-horned and spiral-horned antelopes. The members of this group of bovids are classified into loose tribes rather than formal subgroups, as the evolutionary relationships within the groups are still uncertain. General characteristics include cloven hooves and usually at least one of the sexes of a species having true horns. The largest extant bovine is the gaur."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Buffalo_and_Oxpeckers_%287234007684%29.jpg/330px-Buffalo_and_Oxpeckers_%287234007684%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bovinae","wikidata":"Q4979192"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg/500px-Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg/1280px-Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg/500px-Bovine_skull_02-FMVZ_USP-20.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bovine skull","li